    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d290">

                <pb facs="0331" n="325" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg325"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.33/445: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hayes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-11-11T20:00:00+01:00">November 11,
                            1942—8 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 12—2:58 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1758. Foreign Office has received telegram summarizing <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> along the lines of Department’s 1166, November 4, 10
                        p.m.<anchor n="83" xml:id="d290-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>It states that the two tankers are already in the inner harbor and the cargo ship
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Bessel</hi> also will be placed there.</p>
                <p>Department’s 888, September 18, 3 p.m.<anchor n="84" xml:id="d290-f2"/> Total
                    naval petroleum stocks as of October 10 were 5,799 tons fuel oil and 580 tons
                    gas oil divided among <hi rendition="#italic">Ferrol, Cádiz, Cartagena, Palma,
                        Mahon, Seller, Crucero, Canarias</hi> and the remaining vessels of the
                    Spanish Fleet.</p>
                <p>A later statement of navy stocks is being prepared. A statement of military
                    stocks has also been requested of the military.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hayes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d290-f1" n="83" xml:id="d290-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram No. 1166 not printed; for <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi>, see
                        <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
